<div class="page-intro">
  <p class="kicker">A standing project · github.com/zorvan/Zwischen</p>
  <h1>Zwischen</h1>
  <p>Coordination for collective life — mediated through perception, not prediction.</p>
</div>

<section>
  <p class="axiom" style="max-width:30ch;margin-bottom:2rem">
    <span class="a1">No modelling of users.</span>
    <span class="a2">No inferring reliability.</span>
    <span class="a3">No steering of outcomes.</span>
  </p>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      <em>Zwischen</em> — German for the <em>in-between</em> — is a coordination system for small
      groups. It shapes how people relate to what is forming: an evening, a match, a gathering. Most
      coordination tools quietly become surveillance — scoring who is reliable, predicting who will
      show, nudging behaviour toward a metric. Zwischen refuses all three. It makes the shared state
      <strong>perceptible</strong> and lets the group act on what it sees.
    </p>
    <p>
      The working core is a Telegram bot: groups form events, track participation and constraints,
      handle waitlists and lifecycles, and — the part that matters most — carry <strong>memory</strong>
      from one gathering into the next. Built in Python on <code>python-telegram-bot</code>,
      SQLAlchemy, and PostgreSQL, with a Mini App and a standalone client on the roadmap.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="ledger" aria-label="Form, Participate, Surface, Carry">
    <div class="cell">
      <p class="step">01 — Form</p>
      <p class="what">Event</p>
      <p class="gloss">A gathering takes shape — time, place, the shape of the ask.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cell">
      <p class="step">02 — Participate</p>
      <p class="what">Commitment</p>
      <p class="gloss">People join, decline, or wait; constraints are held honestly.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cell">
      <p class="step">03 — Surface</p>
      <p class="what">Perception</p>
      <p class="gloss">Coordination state is made visible — no scores, no predictions.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cell">
      <p class="step">04 — Carry</p>
      <p class="what">Memory</p>
      <p class="gloss">What happened travels forward into the next gathering.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

